From: awto <noreply@awto.au>
Subject: [PATCH] community rules: explicit arm64 read syscalls instead of perm=r (awto-unvr #358)

libaudit expands perm=r to readlink,stat,open,...; arm64 has none of the legacy ones so augenrules fails and no rules load.
---
diff --git a/rules/truenas-community-edition.rules b/rules/truenas-community-edition.rules
index 0f31a9b..c8079ec 100644
--- a/rules/truenas-community-edition.rules
+++ b/rules/truenas-community-edition.rules
@@ -12,4 +12,6 @@
 -A exclude,always -F msgtype=SERVICE_STOP
 
 ## TrueNAS configuration
--a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/data/ -F perm=r -F auid!=unset -F key=escalation
+## awto-unvr: no perm=r - libaudit expands it to readlink,stat,open,... which arm64 lacks (augenrules fails).
+## Explicit arm64-valid read syscalls (generic table; no open/stat/lstat/readlink).
+-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -S openat,openat2,readlinkat,newfstatat,fstat,statx,listxattr,llistxattr,flistxattr,getxattr,lgetxattr,fgetxattr,quotactl -F dir=/data/ -F auid!=unset -F key=escalation
